cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this audit or its Lean certificates, please cite the versioned release."
type: software
title: "A Lean-checked parameter audit for exact discrete Fourier transforms"
version: "0.2.32"
date-released: "2026-10-08"
authors:
  - name: "QZP"
abstract: >-
  Lean-checked arithmetic and local frame certificates for a parameter audit
  of the unrestricted-coefficient exact discrete Fourier transform recurrence.
  The release records finite-network and conditional research candidates and
  explicitly leaves the complete all-length frame-labelled recursion open.
  It also records the concrete Walsh-frame commutation lemma for orthogonal
  binary address changes, a nondegenerate one-coordinate projected-phase
  instance, a two-coordinate nested residual of rank one, and normalized
  Walsh framed-phase composition identities.  This version adds a formal
  q-free side-moment reuse identity, exact fixed-coordinate incidence-rank
  certificates, and an H18 local frame build audit.  This version additionally
  attaches the reuse identity to supplied finite-prefix frame schedules and
  parameterizes the fused-centre normalized arithmetic.  This version also
  records the conditional zero-auxiliary-charge ledger obtained when the
  q-free side correction reuses the centre frame; all of these remain local or
  conditional certificates and do not by themselves provide a global gate
  schedule.  This version also adds an independent exact Python audit of the
  reused H24 role count, padding bucket, and direct-diagonal margin, a
  conditional parity-split finite-schedule bridge, and a scoped
  finite-dimensional obstruction to lower-rank additive direct factorizations.
  This version generalizes the target-boundary intersection no-go to every
  h greater than or equal to four and adds an exact h-parameter padding-bucket
  scan, including the conditional h=30 improvement and its negative direct
  channel margin.  It also formalizes the minimal four-singleton target cover
  and, for even h, an arbitrary dense two-label cover using e_0 and 1+e_0;
  both are label-level certificates and leave gate realization, scheduling,
  and the all-length recurrence open.  The singleton minimality certificate
  is independently buildable after removing a duplicate imported abbreviation.
repository-code: "https://github.com/whyihaveyou/math"
